 "note": [
  "Scripture is the Open Word Bible (OWB), Balanced edition, Japanese (owb-ja, bundled), per the 2026-11-19 founder decision; this edition was re-quoted from the 口語訳 in one pass, every quotation checked against the English and the OWB text.",
  "Self-rendered rows added in the re-quote, with why OWB could not serve: Matthew 14:30 (ch1 b17): Moody's conflation: 'Lord, save me, or I perish' (Matt 14:30 + 8:25), not one verse; Luke 18:11 (ch3 b14): OWB sets the Pharisee's list mid-sentence ('…でなく…ことを、感謝します'); no clean excerpt for 'I thank Thee that I am not as other men are'; Psalm 35:13 (ch4 b15): the KJV idiom 'my prayer returned into mine own bosom' has no counterpart in OWB's rendering; Job 1:21 (ch5 b10): Thomas Adams's paraphrase of Job 1:21, not a quotation; Matthew 6:10 (ch6 b2): Moody's own sentence ('God's will is not done here'), an allusion; Luke 7:6-7 (ch8 b21): Moody's paraphrase of the centurion's message, not a quotation; Mark 11:22 (ch8 b31): title of the closing hymn ('Have faith in God'), kept with the verse translation; 1 John 5:4 (ch8 b26): Rutherford's paraphrase ('this is our victory'), an allusion; Deuteronomy 34:6 (ch10 b6): Moody's point ('God buried him') rests on the KJV's active subject; OWB has the passive '葬られた' with no subject; Matthew 26:42 (ch10 b17): hymn refrain ('Thy will be done!') kept in the verse translation's metre; Acts 26:28 (ch11 b36): 'almost persuaded' is the hymn phrase; OWB renders Agrippa's words differently; Galatians 6:14 (ch11 b42): 'God forbid that I should glory' is the speaker's echo turned to his own shame, an allusion. The older self_rendered rows without chapter_order are the first translation's allusions and paraphrases, kept as they were."
 ],
